[SECTION 9] PYTHON CONCEPTS
1. DECORATOR Function takes another function adds functionality returns new function Syntax @decorator_name def my_func(): ... Example def my_decorator(func): def wrapper(): print("Before") func() print("After") return wrapper @my_decorator def say_hello(): print("Hello Binance $81,228") In Flask @app.route('/api/price') adds routing
2. jsonify Converts Python dict to JSON HTTP response Without jsonify return {"price":81228} TypeError With jsonify return jsonify({"price":81228}) Content-Type application/json Frontend fetch().then(r=>r.json())
3. CORS Browser security Frontend https://hyarelgits.github.io/ai1/ calls http://localhost:5000/api/price blocks CORS header Access-Control-Allow-Origin * Flask CORS(app) adds header Without CORS Error CORS policy No Access-Control-Allow-Origin
4. Flask Lightweight Python web framework Alternative Django heavy Basics from flask import Flask app=Flask(__name__) @app.route('/') def home():return "Hi" app.run() Microframework
5. MVC Model View Controller Model Data Logic Binance API $81,228 SL $80,600 CVD +$12.4M View What user sees index.html 7 tabs TradingView +$409 Controller Connects Model View @app.route JS fetch Benefit Change View without touching Model
6. host='0.0.0.0' vs '127.0.0.1' 127.0.0.1 Only same machine Secure dev 0.0.0.0 All interfaces Allows VM host phone access For Ubuntu VM training Use 0.0.0.0
7. port=5000 Port door number 80 HTTP 443 HTTPS 5000 Flask dev If busy Address already in use Change 5001 or kill lsof -i :5000 kill -9 PID
8. requests library To call external API Binance requests.get(url) fetches data Alternative urllib

